<reference id="monthly-inspection-record-for-asset" xml:lang="en">
<title>Monthly inspection record for <ph keyref="asset">feed pump B</ph></title>
<shortdesc>The record a technician completes during the monthly inspection of <ph keyref="asset">feed pump B</ph>, tag <ph keyref="tag">PS-104</ph>, under procedure MP-PS104-01. The maintenance console fills the first table from the work order; the technician fills the rest. A record is complete when every field has a value or the entry <b>Not applicable</b>, and the supervisor has signed it. Fictional sample written for this portfolio: it isn't a record for real equipment.</shortdesc>
<refbody>
<section><title>Work order</title>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>Field</stentry><stentry>Value</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry>Work order</stentry><stentry>From the console</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Asset</stentry><stentry><ph keyref="asset">feed pump B</ph>, tag <ph keyref="tag">PS-104</ph></stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Location</stentry><stentry>Pump room 2, east bay</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Procedure</stentry><stentry>MP-PS104-01, version 0.3</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Scheduled date</stentry><stentry>From the console</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Technician</stentry><stentry>Name and badge number</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Shift</stentry><stentry>Day or night</stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
<section><title>Conditions at the start</title>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>Field</stentry><stentry>Value</stentry><stentry>Unit</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry>Pump running at normal load</stentry><stentry>Yes or no</stentry><stentry></stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Ambient temperature in the pump room</stentry><stentry></stentry><stentry>°C</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Running hours since the last inspection</stentry><stentry>From the console</stentry><stentry>h</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Alarms active on the console</stentry><stentry>None, or list them</stentry><stentry></stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
<section><title>Readings</title>
<p>Take each reading as the procedure describes, and enter it before you take the next one. Enter the value you read, not the value you expect.</p>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>Check</stentry><stentry>Reading</stentry><stentry>Unit</stentry><stentry>Expected</stentry><stentry>Inside range</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry>Discharge pressure</stentry><stentry></stentry><stentry>bar</stentry><stentry>3.8 to 4.6</stentry><stentry>Yes or no</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Bearing temperature, drive end</stentry><stentry></stentry><stentry>°C</stentry><stentry>Below 70</stentry><stentry>Yes or no</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Vibration, drive-end bearing housing</stentry><stentry></stentry><stentry>mm/s</stentry><stentry>Below 4.5</stentry><stentry>Yes or no</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Seal leakage</stentry><stentry>None, drip, or stream</stentry><stentry></stentry><stentry>None visible</stentry><stentry>Yes or no</stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
<section><title>Observations</title>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>Item</stentry><stentry>Finding</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry>Unusual noise</stentry><stentry>None, or describe it</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Coupling guard in place and secure</stentry><stentry>Yes or no</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Base bolts tight, no visible movement</stentry><stentry>Yes or no</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Oil level in the sight glass</stentry><stentry>Low, normal, or high</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Corrosion or paint damage</stentry><stentry>None, or describe it</stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
<section><title>Outcome</title>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>Field</stentry><stentry>Value</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry>All readings inside range</stentry><stentry>Yes or no</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Work order closed</stentry><stentry>Yes or no</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Reported to the shift supervisor</stentry><stentry>Not needed, or the time and the reading reported</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Follow-up work order raised</stentry><stentry>None, or its number</stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
<section><title>Sign-off</title>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>Role</stentry><stentry>Name</stentry><stentry>Date</stentry><stentry>Signature</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry>Technician</stentry><stentry></stentry><stentry></stentry><stentry></stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Shift supervisor</stentry><stentry></stentry><stentry></stentry><stentry></stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
<section><title>Retention</title>
<p>The console keeps the record with the work order for the life of the asset. A paper copy, if one is used, goes to the maintenance office at the end of the shift and is scanned within a week.</p>
</section>
</refbody>
</reference>
